        "original_id": "7ad3735d-1b7c-50b8-add7-689c2dafe8b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elissa Schappell, Oprah Winfrey, Holly MacArthur, Rob Spillman, Melissa Broder\n- Organizations: Newsweek/The Daily Beast, Hearst Communications\n- Publications: O, The Oprah Magazine, Tin House, Last Sext, So Sad Today\n- Topics: magazines, editing, publishing, social media\n\nFacts:\n- O, The Oprah Magazine is a monthly magazine founded by Oprah Winfrey and Hearst Communications and is primarily marketed at women.\n- Tin House was developed with help from New York editors Rob Spillman and Elissa Schappell, and Holly MacArthur was enlisted as managing editor.\n- Elissa Schappell is associated with Newsweek/The Daily Beast and O Magazine.\n- Melissa Broder's 2016 works include the poetry collection Last Sext from Tin House and the essay collection So Sad Today from Grand Central.\n- Melissa Broder also created a popular Twitter feed titled So Sad Today, on which the book So Sad Today is based.",
